# core2ai Build

`@core2ai/core` exports **`out/`** (compiled JS), not `src/`. Consumers resolve it via **`npm link`** — the symlink stays valid; only **`out/`** must stay current.

## One-time link setup

```bash
# core2ai
npm run build && npm link

# api2ai or db2ai (from repo root)
cd packages/cli && npm link @core2ai/core && cd ../..
npm install
cd packages/extension/demos && npm link @core2ai/core && npm install
```

Verify: `ls -l node_modules/@core2ai/core` → symlink to sibling `../core2ai`.

## After every change under `src/codegen/**`

Pick one:

| Mode | Command | When |
|------|---------|------|
| **Active editing** | `npm run watch` in **core2ai** (runs `tsc --watch`) | Saves recompile to `out/` automatically — **recommended** while hacking core2ai |
| **Occasional change** | `npm run build` in **core2ai** | Enough if you change core2ai rarely |

**No** consumer `npm link` again after rebuild — symlink already points at the repo; updated files land in `out/`.

Optional sanity: `npm run check` in **core2ai** before switching to a consumer.

## What consumers still need (depends on what you changed)

| Change in core2ai | Consumer action |
|-------------------|-----------------|
| **codegen** (generator helpers, `renderMcpServeSource`) | Regenerate demos if MCP bootstrap shape changed: `generate:all`, `build:generated`; **restart MCP** in Cursor |
| **Extension / VSIX embed** | `npm run build` in `packages/extension` (re-runs `embed-cli-bundle.mjs`) — link alone does **not** update bundled `cli.cjs` |

See [generated-output-do-not-edit.mdc](./generated-output-do-not-edit.mdc).

## Do not

- Edit `out/` by hand — always `src/` → `npm run build` or `npm run watch`
- `cp` into `node_modules/@core2ai/core`
- Rely on GitHub pin / registry (local dev uses **npm link** only)
